    "narrative": "Today\u2019s roster for the Austin Waves features a balanced attack, anchored by the elite 83.29 efficiency score of **Gunnar Henderson**. Facing a favorable matchup against the right-handed arm of G. Holmes, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a perfect storm of park factors (+16%) and a strong platoon advantage (+14%), making him our most reliable engine for R, HR, and RBI production. **Drake Baldwin** (72.68) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.88) also grade out as top-tier starts; **Drake Baldwin** is buoyed by an ideal leadoff spot and a 0.390 xwOBA, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a favorable park adjustment and his primary spot in the heart of the order. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** (68.36) remains a high-floor play, gaining marginal utility from an opposing pitcher's slow delivery, which provides a necessary boost to our pursuit of scarce stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision today involved **Luis Lara**, whose 54.02 score nearly cracked the lineup. While **Luis Lara** benefits from a strong SP_xERA matchup, he was ultimately edged out by **Heliot Ramos** (66.08), who offers a superior ceiling due to wind-assisted power potential and a dynamic platoon advantage. We are keeping a close watch on **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Andy Pages**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Liam Hicks**, all of whom are currently projected based on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Should official lineups shift these players down in the batting order, their efficiency scores will likely regress. Risk is currently centered on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose raw projection is strong but is hampered by a significant -15% dynamic platoon penalty against the left-handed Rodriguez. While we have depth options like **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Cole Carrigg** held in reserve, the current volatility of the bottom-third of the order necessitates that we monitor pre-game reports to ensure we aren't leaving points on the table by starting players who are potentially platooned out of the official lineup.",
